\chapter{From Canvas assignments to FBF activities}
\label{Canvas}

Users think in Canvas terms: a course, an assignment.
FBF has its own: an LTI course and an activity, each with a UUID.
This chapter connects the two, so that the commands can take the familiar
[[canvaslms]] options [[-c]] and [[-a]] and work on the corresponding FBF
activities.

The connection is the launch URL of the assignment.
An FBF assignment in Canvas launches
[[https://api.feedbackfruits.com/v1/lti/launch?code=...]], and the [[code]]
identifies the FBF \emph{placement} of the activity, that is, where in Canvas
it sits.
FBF's placement resource carries the same code and points to the activity.
So one launch per Canvas course gives us a token and that course's FBF
course, and the codes give us its activities without further launches.
Two things complicate the picture, and the sections below deal with them:
a code is shared by all the course rounds that copied the assignment, and
a launch may create an activity.

